    <string name="ajustes_cuenta_borrada_ultima">You were the last person with an account in this family. Its information is still saved. Write down this code: whoever enters it when creating their account will be linked to your person and carry on with everything.\n\n%1$s</string>
    <string name="ajustes_cuenta_borrada_texto">Your account has been deleted. The family\'s information is still saved.</string>
    <string name="ajustes_borrar_titulo">Delete your account?</string>
    <string name="ajustes_borrar_texto">Your account will be removed from the app and you\'ll lose access to this family and stop receiving alerts. Your person and their whole history stay in the family, and someone else can be linked to them again. This can\'t be undone.</string>
    <string name="ajustes_borrar_accion">Delete</string>
    <string name="ajustes_error_borrar_cuenta">Couldn\'t delete the account. Check your connection and try again.</string>
    <string name="ajustes_error_desvincular">Couldn\'t unlink the account. Please try again.</string>
    <string name="ajustes_alarma_titulo">Alerts may arrive late</string>
    <string name="ajustes_alarma_texto">%1$s isn\'t allowed to schedule alarms at an exact time, so your phone may delay activity alerts by several minutes. To make them go off exactly on time, turn on “Alarms &amp; reminders” for %1$s.</string>
    <string name="ajustes_activar">Turn on</string>
    <string name="bateria_titulo">Alerts with the app closed</string>
    <string name="bateria_sin_restricciones">%1$s has no battery restrictions. If alerts still don\'t reach you with the app closed, your phone may have its own manufacturer power saving.</string>
    <string name="bateria_con_restricciones">Your phone\'s battery saver can stop alerts from arriving when %1$s isn\'t open on screen. To avoid this, remove the battery restrictions: the %1$s settings page will open. Go to “Battery” and choose “Unrestricted” (depending on your phone, it may be called “Don\'t optimize”).</string>
